      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1309932898">
          <groundspeak:date>2025-07-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP312 Wedding Cap [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This one is sure not flush with the ground any more; I’d heard new grass has been put in over the last few years and that would seem to be the case. But I swept, swept, swept and eventually got a buzz, and then I started digging. If anyone else comes looking for this soon (yeah right) their task should be a lot easier. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I’m attaching my boring picture of a water bottle in the middle of some grass. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684127530">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP312 Wedding Cap.  First time for me in this area.  No weddings this early in the morning but the cap was a quick find.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
